ng tests); a seventh exit code for a failure after the send (the stdout lines carry the difference); deleting what the command created when the engine refuses (a deletion in the user's directory on an error path). Trade-off: the user must state a ceiling and the consent details on every real run; a store the probe cannot judge (a corrupt database) is found after the key was read and the call log was opened, still before any request (Ambiguity 8); the recovery file is outside the store and outside deletion and retention (BL-240). Tests: `test_dry_run_sends_nothing_and_prints_plan`, `test_audit_f4_the_dry_run_prints_the_cap_check`, `test_audit_f4_sarvam_needs_an_explicit_ceiling`, `test_audit_f4_a_plan_over_the_ceiling_is_refused_before_any_engine_or_request`, `test_audit_f5_sarvam_is_refused_unless_consent_is_obtained`, `test_audit_f5_the_reference_is_never_printed_or_reported_only_stored`, `test_audit_f2_the_store_is_open_and_the_directory_exists_before_the_engine_is_called`, `test_audit_f2_the_export_is_checked_against_the_alignment_cap_before_the_send`, `test_audit_f2_a_store_failure_after_the_send_keeps_the_usage_and_writes_the_report`, `test_audit_f2_a_missing_key_still_leaves_no_directory_behind`.
